native arm64 backend's emitCallFuncValue arg-marshaling doesn't match the per-function `__shim.<mangled>` shim's signature when the user function takes a 16-byte slice value (i.e. *[]T / @[]T).  The shim expects the slice as 2 args (data, len) starting at the data-slot offset, but the call site passes only one register.  Output is empty (the called function reads garbage for the slice length so the for-loop body never runs).  See "Native AArch64 backend — emitCallFuncValue slice-arg ABI mismatch" in explorations/claude-todo.md.
